  "body": "It seems that some Primary services are mistakenly listed as Secondary (the indication I get from the bluetooth inspector - including snapshot).\r\n\r\n![image](https://github.com/WebBluetoothCG/web-bluetooth/assets/1014678/8438ed6d-1474-48b8-88d2-c98000c40d44)\r\n\r\nOS: Ubuntu Linux 22.04.2 LTS (Jammy Jellyfish)\r\nChrome: 114.0.5735.198\r\nBlueZ: 5.64\r\n\r\nSample exposing problem: https://larsgk.github.io/genericsensor-thingy52/\r\nError thrown: \r\n`Uncaught (in promise) DOMException: No Services matching UUID ef680400-9b35-4933-9b10-52ffa9740042 found in Device.`\r\n\r\nThe linked sample has worked find on the same laptop previously.  I am not sure what BlueZ and Chrome combination I saw working last.  The sample also works fine on my Android 13, Chrome 115.0.5790.138",
